    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup today is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our highest efficiency score of 83.29. Facing Canning, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive park factor boost (+16%) and a favorable platoon matchup, positioning him as the primary engine for our Roto categories today. Joining him in the elite tier is **Kyle Tucker** (77.91), who maintains high value despite a lingering \"Lineup Pending\" status; his underlying skills versus lefties and a favorable wind forecast make him an automatic start. **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) remains a critical component of today's strategy, not only for his 75.10 score but for his stolen base potential against Baz, whose slow delivery provides the exact high-efficiency environment we need to exploit our focus on the scarcest category.\n\nTactically, we are leaning into aggressive platoon advantages to bolster our efficiency. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (64.20) and **Andy Pages** (75.18) provide strong production against their respective opponents, while **Sam Antonacci** (63.13) and **Miguel Vargas** (61.69) are prioritized against Roki Sasaki due to the combination of favorable wind conditions and, in the case of **Miguel Vargas**, the high probability of a stolen base attempt against the pitcher's delivery tempo. The most difficult decision on the bench was **Josh Jung**, who landed at a 55.18 score. While his park factors against Gray are appealing, he was ultimately squeezed out by the sheer efficiency density of the outfield and middle-infield options currently rostered. \n\nA final note of caution: we are carrying significant risk with our \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Kyle Tucker**, **Andy Pages**, and **Dominic Smith**. While their projections remain high, any late-breaking news regarding rest or a demotion in the batting order could necessitate a pivot to the bench, where **Nolan Schanuel** and **Wade Meckler** are waiting in the wings. We will monitor the clubhouse reports 